<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Australian retail sales fall 1.7 pct in April.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Australian retail sales fall 1.7 pct in April.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-05-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australian retail sales fell 1.7 percent to A$10.29 billion in April, seasonally adjusted, after falling 0.3 percent to A$10.46 billion in March, the Australian Bureau of Statistics said.</p>
<p>In April 1996, retail sales fell 0.6 percent to A$10.13 billion.</p>
<p>Analysts median expectations had centred on a rise of 0.5 percent for April.  </p>
<p>Australian retail sales, April 1997 (A$ billion)</p>
<p>			   April 97 March 97 m/m pct April 96  y/y pct</p>
<p>    Seasonally adj    10.29    10.46   -1.7     10.13    +1.5</p>
<p>    Unadjusted	   9.96    10.03   -0.8	9.73    +2.3</p>
<p>    Trend Estimates   10.44    10.42   +0.2     10.20    +2.3</p>
